# regions.sh: the review's checker repros the checker ACCEPTS today and
# that fail under ASan+UBSan -- the one region judgement of
# docs/region-plan.md is to refuse each (2026-10-21).  A line here must
# still be accepted and still fail; a program not here must be refused.
# (the families -- C1 to C4 -- are the review's; which repro is which is
#  in docs/compiler-review-2026-10-21.md, Part 2)
# 2026-10-21: the FRAME family switched over (plan, step 5) -- A1, A1b,
# A3, A4, A4a, A4b, A5, B2, B2b, B3, B3c refused by the region
# judgement; D3 and E1 by the OLD analyses, whose memoised summaries
# answer by visit order (the review's C3) and are now asked first by the
# region walk -- an accident of that order, removed with the summaries
# by SCC.  The READ-ONLY family the same day: E2-E10 refused.
# RETENTION and RETURN the next day (2026-10-22), once the answer
# summaries removed the three imprecise findings: K1a refused.  The list
# is empty: every one of the review's 24 is refused.
# 2026-10-25: W1, an RO answer stored in an ELEMENT of a record's field
# and written through it (`o.names[0] := Pick ('abc') ; o.names[0][0]
# := 'X'`) -- the judgement tracks x.f and x[].f, not x.f[]; found
# testing the table's size, accepted by 0.24 and 0.25 alike, SIGBUS --
# refused the same evening: a field's element is judged by what was
# stored into the field, as a bare name's is.  The list is empty again.
# 2026-10-26: the second review's region holes, accepted by 0.25.0 and
# unsafe under the sanitizers (docs/compiler-review-2026-10-26.md),
# refused before they were added, so none is owed: R2N04/R2N04b/R2N21/
# R2N21b/R2N27 a call-selection F (x).f, R2N05/R2N05b/R2N05c a loop the
# fixpoint gave up on after 9 passes, R2N06/R2N07/R2N13/R2N14 a SLICE of
# a local ARRAY escaping, R2N23 a GRID over a literal in a record field,
# R2N37/R2N38 an IS SOME binder in a WHILE and an ELSIF.
# The same night's second batch, refused before added: R2N39 a literal
# lent to a VAR STR the callee writes through (S5), R2G19 an element of
# a by-value slice handed to a VAR STR, which the callee re-homed into
# the frame (gen N4), R2F04/R2F04b a record answer whose aggregate holds
# a frame string, its field kept (fuzz N4).
# 2026-10-26, tier 1 of the third review, refused before added: R3Cyc3 a
# three-procedure cycle accepted in 288 of its 720 declaration orders
# (the memo's busy entries; iteration at a cycle's head now), R3K48 a
# KEPT parameter past the 48th (the judgement failed open), R3RoField a
# literal in a record field lent to a VAR STR the callee writes
# through, R3DisposeModVar (was sanitize/SanDisposeModVar) DISPOSE of a
# borrowed answer in the module body.
# 2026-10-26, tier 2 (read-only storage by depth): R3Depth3 a write of a
# literal's octets two levels down; R3DepthAlias and R3DepthBack the same
# through `rows[0] := row' with the literal stored through the other
# name afterwards -- SIGBUS, accepted by every compiler before this (the
# flow-sensitive walk copies a name's contents when it is stored, not
# what is stored through either name later; the depth scan, flow-
# insensitive and both ways across the pair, sees it).
# 2026-10-27: an RO RECORD parameter copied whole (`fl := other`), then written
# through a slice it holds into the caller's storage: the copy's tracked
# fields keep their earlier state, so the read-only mark never reaches them.
# REFUSED 2026-10-29 (off the list): a whole copy of read-only storage marks
# the copy's tracked fields read-only; R4CopyBranch, R4CopyLoop,
# R4CopyElem, R4CopyOfField, R4CopyHead refused before they were added.
# 2026-10-28: a pool's storage handed back through VAR parameters into a
# module variable (CLAUDE.md's owed entry, written as a repro the day the
# ownership probe went through the owed list): RStr keeps its POOL
# parameter's copy in its VAR parameter, and the pool is the caller's local.
# REFUSED 2026-10-30 (off the list): Sem.PoolInto, the caller judges a
# callee that stores what it allocates in a POOL parameter into a VAR one
# (decision 83).  The list is empty again.
